# GetStockReport.com - Cursor AI Rules

## Core Project Stack
- Frontend: Next.js (App Router, Standalone Output), Tailwind CSS, React
- Backend: FastAPI (Python 3.12, Uvicorn, Virtualenv at `backend/venv`)
- Database: PostgreSQL (`stockintel`)
- Infra: AWS EC2 (t3.small, Ubuntu 24.04), Nginx (Reverse Proxy), PM2

## Non-Negotiable Rules & Constraints
1. Next.js Build Assets: Every production build MUST copy static assets to the standalone directory (`.next/static` to `.next/standalone/.next/static` and `public` to `.next/standalone/public`).
2. API URL Configuration: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` and `API_PUBLIC_URL` MUST NOT have a trailing `/api` suffix. (e.g., use `https://getstockreport.com`, NOT `https://getstockreport.com/api`).
3. Access Control & Redaction:
   - Free Tier: Max 5 unique reports/month per registered user.
   - Guest/Free Tier Redactions: Sensitive price target and insider numbers must be redacted ON THE BACKEND with `$$$.$$`. Never rely on CSS hiding.
4. Legal Compliance: Never write explicit "buy", "sell", or "hold" recommendations. Use neutral score bands:
   - 75-100: Bullish Consensus
   - 50-74: Mixed Signals
   - 0-49: Bearish Consensus
5. Python Commands: Always run backend python/pip commands inside the virtual environment (`source backend/venv/bin/activate`).
